WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.810
Virtual Conferences.
They put us in the position&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:11.940
to do what we have not done before,&nbsp;
which is giving a pre-recorded talk.&nbsp;

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.670
This video has 7 tips for you on how to&nbsp;
improve your pre-recorded videos, enjoy!

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:22.410
For a researcher, there are&nbsp;
three key points for success:&nbsp;

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:28.680
The ability of speaking, writing and&nbsp;
the values of the presented ideas.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.720
But since you are interested in this topic&nbsp;
of recording talks for a virtual conference,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.550
I assume the two points below are no&nbsp;
problem for you: You just got a written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:45.690
paper accepted for its valuable ideas. So&nbsp;
this video, will be about the first point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:52.140
specifically about your ability to speak and&nbsp;
record a talk for a virtual presentation.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:58.500
I know, research conferences are drawing us&nbsp;
researchers from various corners of the earth and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:06.120
for many of us, English is not a native language.&nbsp;
This is one more reason to speak slowly enough and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.220
most importantly, clearly. Less like this, because&nbsp;
Iam going to talk about my work [unitelligible],

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:12.990
and more like, this:&nbsp;

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:19.230
"Hello there, my name is Letitia Parcalabescu and&nbsp;
I am going to talk to you about Multimodality."

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:23.970
The second point I am going&nbsp;
to talk about, is... smiling!

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.770
You are presenting your work that&nbsp;
just got accepted at a conference,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:34.615
so please do not speak like you are&nbsp;
attending a funeral [funeral song].

00:01:34.615 --> 00:01:37.840
Smile a little and this will&nbsp;
not only enlighten your face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.720
but also your voice will become more pleasant.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.310
Camera specifications are not exactly&nbsp;
the most important issue here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:48.520
because nobody wants to see&nbsp;
all your pores on your face.&nbsp;

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:55.000
But very important is your camera's position.
Many of us record with the laptop camera.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.290
This delivers the perfect angle for&nbsp;
the viewer to inspect your nostrils!

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:04.630
Keep in mind to place the camera aligned&nbsp;
to your face to deliver an optimal result.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.000
Not everyone has a podcast microphone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.880
but consider buying one!
Kidding, kidding!

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:21.690
But whatever microphone you plan to use, do&nbsp;
not choose the oldest iPhone headset lying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:28.140
around in your home, but consider buying a new&nbsp;
one and spending 40€ for a better microphone.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.660
No, they do not pay me for this.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:37.140
It will help you with recording but also in the&nbsp;
numerous Zoom meetings one needs to attend these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:42.840
days. If your microphone does not have always a&nbsp;
white noise or a peeping sound attached to it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:47.880
people will be involuntarily less&nbsp;
disturbed when you are speaking to them!

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:52.200
If your voice and audio are pleasant,&nbsp;
people will be pleasant to you!

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.850
Not all of us are perfect public&nbsp;
speakers and while recording a video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:02.270
there is also no audience hearing you right then.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.780
The lack of audience will not deliver you the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.380
adrenaline that would flow on&nbsp;
a stage while speaking live.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:15.770
So the concentration is of course reduced&nbsp;
while recording. This is why, instead of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:21.470
doing N attempts until you do it all right,&nbsp;
consider doing a minimum of cutting the video.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:27.260
Software like kdenlive is very easy to use&nbsp;
and available for all operating systems!

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:34.250
Possibly an alternative to post-editing&nbsp;
is the compilation of a script to which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.880
you either stick closely or even read from. But it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.780
is very important to do 2 things&nbsp;
if you are working with a script:

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.780
Don't write it like you would write a paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.500
but write it like you would explain&nbsp;
to a colleague what you are doing.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.790
Otherwise, your audience will have&nbsp;
a hard time understanding you.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.840
Secondly, do not forget to interpret this script,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.440
say it like you mean it, like&nbsp;
you would perform in theatre.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.930
And the last tip I have for you:

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:07.820
Relax, if you start some time in advance&nbsp;
before the video hand-in deadline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:13.970
you have a lot of time to&nbsp;
do it until you do it right.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:21.890
And if you are post-editing, do not hesitate&nbsp;
to do it all in one imperfect cut, and then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:25.640
and then repeat the bad parts, and&nbsp;
repeat bad parts like nothing happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:29.240
because you will remove&nbsp;
these in post-editing anyway!

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:34.370
I really hope that this video&nbsp;
helps you record better videos.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.970
I am really curious to read about&nbsp;
your experience in the comments!

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:42.140
Do not forget to hit the&nbsp;
like and subscribe buttons&nbsp;

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.240
and see you next time!

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.040
Ok bye!

